1
00:00:01,130 --> 00:00:03,340
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,930
-[footsteps]
-[HAGURE] Akio's a traitor?

3
00:01:33,010 --> 00:01:34,340
Yup.

4
00:01:34,430 --> 00:01:37,560
[yawns] He tried to kill Asa
but failed big time.

5
00:01:37,890 --> 00:01:39,560
I'm betting
someone on the outside

6
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:41,480
convinced him
to move against us.

7
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,440
We had planned
to grill him and kill him

8
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,900
once the boss man returned.

9
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:46,860
Then everything blew up
in our faces.

10
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:50,820
Seriously, Dad, you think
killing solves everything?

11
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,070
Akio was a major part
of our lives.

12
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,280
Surely we can handle this
without murdering him.

13
00:01:56,370 --> 00:01:57,530
[Gabby sighs]

14
00:01:57,620 --> 00:01:58,700
[inhales]

15
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,330
You say that,

16
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:03,870
but you don't know
the full story.

17
00:02:06,290 --> 00:02:08,090
-[FUYUKI] Kawai, the gardener.
-[gasps]

18
00:02:09,130 --> 00:02:11,630
And those are his daemons
on the floor.

19
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:12,970
They're strays now.

20
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:15,470
[Hagure inhales sharply]

21
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:20,390
Is there anyone here willing
to form a contract with them?

22
00:02:20,470 --> 00:02:22,060
[ALL] Hm...

23
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:25,900
Um...
I'd like to volunteer, please.

24
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:29,150
His daemons were
fairly close to my Heave-Ho.

25
00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:30,610
-I think they'd be compatible...
-[TSUGAI] One, two.

26
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:31,900
...with each other.

27
00:02:41,830 --> 00:02:43,580
-[TSUGAI 1] Three, four.
-[TSUGAI 2] One, two.

28
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:46,040
-[whining]
-One, two.

29
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,000
-[TSUGAI 1] Three, four.
-[TSUGAI 2] One, two.

30
00:02:48,090 --> 00:02:50,250
-One, two.
-[FUYUKI] Excuse me.

31
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:52,920
This pair is called
Gokko-Itachi.

32
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:55,380
No individual names
at the moment.

33
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:58,340
Their previous master
was Sanosuke Kawai.

34
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,560
-He was murdered.
-[squealing]

35
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:04,060
Akio Kuroya killed him
while trying to escape.

36
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:05,890
Still think he should live?

37
00:03:06,350 --> 00:03:08,060
Why would he want
to kill someone

38
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:10,020
who is like family to all of us?

39
00:03:10,110 --> 00:03:11,320
Damn it.

40
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,740
If we were to report this death
to the police,

41
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:15,490
they'd want to investigate
the manor.

42
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:18,740
We'll have to say
he abandoned his job instead.

43
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:22,790
I'm the one who brought Kawai
into the fold.

44
00:03:22,870 --> 00:03:25,250
He had no relatives to speak of.

45
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:27,750
-He'll be easy to erase.
-[gasps]

46
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:29,840
[HAGURE] Jin, no!

47
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:32,630
[breathes shakily]
You can't do this to him.

48
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:35,130
He put in years
of service for us.

49
00:03:35,220 --> 00:03:37,880
At the very least,
he deserves a proper funeral.

50
00:03:37,970 --> 00:03:41,510
What you're proposing
is just heartless. Please, Dad.

51
00:03:42,010 --> 00:03:43,010
Don't do this!

52
00:03:43,970 --> 00:03:45,850
After all, it was
your strict ways

53
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:48,730
that caused Akio
to close himself off to us.

54
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,610
You treat people like family,

55
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:53,610
but you don't think twice
about cutting them out

56
00:03:53,690 --> 00:03:55,490
for the smallest offenses.

57
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:58,450
You kill people
for making a single mistake.

58
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:01,200
If you weren't so stubborn
and opened up your heart,

59
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,490
maybe he would've told us

60
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:04,580
why he thought
he had to betray the clan.

61
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:06,790
What he saw that we didn't.

62
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:08,330
And if he'd done that,

63
00:04:08,410 --> 00:04:11,130
maybe he wouldn't have been
so callous.

64
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:13,960
Maybe Kawai
would still be alive!

65
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,090
Hagure!

66
00:04:15,170 --> 00:04:16,210
[gasps]

67
00:04:17,550 --> 00:04:19,050
[GABBY] Sensei...

68
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:21,850
Do you know why
I like your stories?

69
00:04:21,930 --> 00:04:23,760
There are no bad people in them.

70
00:04:24,970 --> 00:04:27,060
This world sucks big time.

71
00:04:27,140 --> 00:04:28,890
So reading your manga
makes me feel,

72
00:04:28,980 --> 00:04:30,640
I don't know... safe.

73
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:34,270
The people you create
would never try to hurt me

74
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:36,190
or want to get rid of me.

75
00:04:36,780 --> 00:04:39,990
A happy fantasy world
sounds pretty nice right now,

76
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:43,200
because our reality is full
of unbelievably shitty people

77
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:45,490
doing awful things
to one another.

78
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:47,200
Myself included.

79
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:50,120
Still, I'll do everything
in my power

80
00:04:50,210 --> 00:04:53,380
to protect the Kagemori clan
because it's where I belong.

81
00:04:54,130 --> 00:04:56,670
I want you to keep
drawing your cute little stories

82
00:04:56,750 --> 00:04:58,630
in a place you feel safe.

83
00:04:59,510 --> 00:05:03,220
And I want Asa to live a normal,
peaceful life.

84
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,890
Akio chose the parents
who abandoned him

85
00:05:06,970 --> 00:05:08,640
over the people who gave him
a home.

86
00:05:08,730 --> 00:05:10,730
He betrayed those
who cared about him.

87
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:13,610
I don't know how important
his blood family was to him,

88
00:05:13,690 --> 00:05:15,360
but I won't forgive
anyone who tries

89
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,440
to destroy this clan.

90
00:05:17,530 --> 00:05:21,320
I would kill my own parents
if they tried to do that,

91
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,450
with no hesitation.

92
00:05:23,530 --> 00:05:26,700
You can be lenient with assholes
and hope they'll change,

93
00:05:26,790 --> 00:05:28,910
but that rarely ever happens,

94
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
which is why
your only good option

95
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,880
is to take them out
before it's too late.

96
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:36,040
That's the real world.

97
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:38,880
Please forgive me.

98
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,630
[gasps] Asa?

99
00:05:40,710 --> 00:05:43,430
Gabby, do not let her go off
alone by herself!

100
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:46,970
Yeah, I know.
Damn it, Asa! Wait!

101
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:48,810
[BUNBUN] Hey, Haruo?

102
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:52,060
Why is it that human beings
turn on their friends?

103
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:55,940
No daemon would ever
betray their partner.

104
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,230
[Haruo sighs]

105
00:05:58,190 --> 00:05:59,400
[GABBY] Get back here.

106
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,320
You can't run off by yourself.

107
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:03,610
Akio could
still be hiding out here.

108
00:06:04,410 --> 00:06:05,620
Asa!

109
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:09,160
[ASA] Kawai is dead.
And for what?

110
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:12,290
I'm the one Akio wanted to kill.

111
00:06:12,370 --> 00:06:15,750
Kawai wasn't his enemy,
or even a fighter.

112
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:18,250
If his hands were dirty,
it was with soil,

113
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,750
not with someone's blood.

114
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:22,880
He was a normal man
who didn't wish death on anyone.

115
00:06:22,970 --> 00:06:25,630
He was just trying
to live his life!

116
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,260
It's my fault.

117
00:06:28,350 --> 00:06:29,970
[grunts] Idiot!

118
00:06:31,930 --> 00:06:34,940
No, it isn't!
The people to blame are the ones

119
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:36,810
who want to exploit
all your power.

120
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:39,320
What happened isn't your fault,
damn it.

121
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:42,110
Didn't Yuru tell you to stop
saying sorry for everything?

122
00:06:42,190 --> 00:06:45,530
Apologize for dumb shit again
and I'll kick your ass.

123
00:06:45,610 --> 00:06:47,700
More than I already have.

124
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:50,870
[Asa whimpers, cries]

125
00:06:50,950 --> 00:06:52,500
[ASA] I'm sorry, Gabby.

126
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:53,750
[Gabby grunts]

127
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,170
What did I just say?

128
00:06:56,330 --> 00:06:57,460
♪

129
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:00,380
[scraping]

130
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:03,800
[grunting]

131
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:18,560
[gasps]

132
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:25,530
[breathing uneasily]

133
00:07:29,410 --> 00:07:30,410
[sighs]

134
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:35,660
Father's... not here.

135
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,210
I'm on my own.

136
00:07:38,750 --> 00:07:41,840
I need to clean
this mess up all by myself.

137
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,170
I have to.

138
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:45,970
[grunting]
This bandit tried to kill me.

139
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:50,720
So I can't hesitate to act!

140
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,810
[grunts]

141
00:07:52,810 --> 00:07:55,680
[panting]

142
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:02,900
Do what needs to be done.

143
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:04,230
Don't waver.

144
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:06,030
No one's coming to help.

145
00:08:06,530 --> 00:08:08,860
Nobody's going
to fix anything for me.

146
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,450
This is the only way.

147
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:15,540
Out here...

148
00:08:18,830 --> 00:08:20,170
I'm alone.

149
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,710
[Yuru breathes softly]

150
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:26,590
Uh?

151
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,590
Hold on. Where am I?

152
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:32,180
Oh, right.

153
00:08:32,890 --> 00:08:35,010
I fell asleep
in the futon closet.

154
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,350
[gasps]

155
00:08:37,430 --> 00:08:39,940
[LEFT] Ah, are you faring well,
Yuru?

156
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,060
Huh?

157
00:08:41,150 --> 00:08:43,270
You scared
the crap out of me, Left!

158
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,320
[Right chuckles]

159
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:45,690
So, what are you doing
down there?

160
00:08:45,770 --> 00:08:46,780
[LEFT] Guarding you.

161
00:08:47,570 --> 00:08:49,900
-My mobility is still limited...
-Yup!

162
00:08:49,990 --> 00:08:51,780
...but I can keep
a watchful eye on you

163
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:53,200
from this spot on the floor.

164
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:55,580
[YURU] Wonderful. Thanks.

165
00:08:56,660 --> 00:08:59,960
Uh? Hey, you're awake.
Are you feeling any better?

166
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,540
Yeah, I'm not as sluggish.

167
00:09:02,630 --> 00:09:04,170
Do you know what time it is?

168
00:09:04,250 --> 00:09:06,040
[KEN] A little past noon.

169
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:07,960
Huh?

170
00:09:08,050 --> 00:09:11,340
Good morning.
Or afternoon, I guess.

171
00:09:11,430 --> 00:09:13,260
You're not near as pale
as you were.

172
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:15,600
I was scared. Are you all right?

173
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:18,430
-How is your shoulder?
-And fever.

174
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:20,020
You must be on the mend.

175
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,980
-I'm so glad.
-[neighs]

176
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:23,940
[Yuru sighs]

177
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:28,650
[YURU] Hm?

178
00:09:29,650 --> 00:09:30,740
[Yuru screams]

179
00:09:32,450 --> 00:09:34,120
What was that for?

180
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:35,870
So, did you sleep okay?

181
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:38,700
[groans] I had some
less than pleasant dreams.

182
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:40,160
[HANA] Oh, dang.

183
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:42,660
Well, have some food
and try to forget them.

184
00:09:42,750 --> 00:09:45,170
Good idea.
I'll whip us up a late lunch.

185
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:48,090
-[Right chuckles]
-We can eat together.

186
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:49,420
Sound good?

187
00:09:50,510 --> 00:09:53,090
[footsteps]

188
00:10:04,190 --> 00:10:06,190
[GABBY] Took you
long enough, Jinny.

189
00:10:06,270 --> 00:10:07,730
Could you clean this up?

190
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:12,570
Were they
Higashi Village agents?

191
00:10:12,650 --> 00:10:16,950
Gotta be. Just look.
They managed to kill Asa.

192
00:10:17,030 --> 00:10:18,240
[Jin breathes uneasily]

193
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:23,000
[GABBY] Our girl died
and gained the power of Break.

194
00:10:24,920 --> 00:10:26,330
[ASA] Jin...

195
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:28,540
I'm sorry. [cries]

196
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:32,340
I'm sorry you have
to clean this up.

197
00:10:32,420 --> 00:10:34,090
It's my fault.

198
00:10:34,930 --> 00:10:36,220
I'm sorry.

199
00:10:37,350 --> 00:10:38,600
I'm sorry.

200
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:40,100
I'm sorry.

201
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:42,730
I'm... sorry.

202
00:10:42,810 --> 00:10:44,350
I'm sorry. Huh?

203
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:50,400
Think nothing of it.

204
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:53,190
Cleaning up messes
is my job, after all.

205
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:55,860
There's nothing
that you need to apologize for.

206
00:10:55,950 --> 00:10:57,740
I'll handle this.

207
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:00,910
You get some rest
and let your mind at ease.

208
00:11:00,990 --> 00:11:02,410
[Asa gasps]

209
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:07,460
[snoring]

210
00:11:10,790 --> 00:11:13,130
-[ASA] Gabs, you're heavy.
-[groaning]

211
00:11:15,090 --> 00:11:16,630
[GABBY] How did you sleep?

212
00:11:20,050 --> 00:11:21,140
Not great.

213
00:11:21,810 --> 00:11:23,680
I had some bad dreams.

214
00:11:23,770 --> 00:11:25,390
That's lame.

215
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:28,150
Grab something to eat
and forget about them.

216
00:11:28,810 --> 00:11:31,770
Wonder if there's
anything tasty in the kitchen.

217
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:33,110
[birds chirping]

218
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:36,360
Good morning.
Or afternoon, rather.

219
00:11:36,450 --> 00:11:37,910
What are you doing here?

220
00:11:37,990 --> 00:11:40,240
Please tell me you haven't
been keeping watch.

221
00:11:40,330 --> 00:11:43,200
I worried someone would strike
thinking our guard was down.

222
00:11:43,290 --> 00:11:45,410
As if we wouldn't expect
another attack.

223
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:47,210
But I didn't hear a peep
the whole night.

224
00:11:47,290 --> 00:11:48,580
[ASA] The whole night?

225
00:11:48,670 --> 00:11:49,670
[NATSUKI] Mm.

226
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,710
I'm gonna go take a shower.

227
00:11:51,790 --> 00:11:53,130
Watch her for me,
will you, Gabby?

228
00:11:53,210 --> 00:11:54,460
Duh-doy!

229
00:11:54,550 --> 00:11:55,800
Hey, Natsuki, wait.

230
00:11:56,470 --> 00:11:57,470
[ALL] Hm?

231
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:58,930
I'm sorry--

232
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:01,260
[Gabby grunting]

233
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:04,770
Thanks for being
so on top of it.

234
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:06,100
[Natsuki chuckles]

235
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:08,810
I'll come back
when I'm done showering.

236
00:12:08,890 --> 00:12:11,610
And then we'll begin
math lessons as usual.

237
00:12:11,690 --> 00:12:12,820
What?

238
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:14,940
Can't she get a single day
to rest up?

239
00:12:15,030 --> 00:12:18,610
[BABAMARU] Staying up all night
is bad for your skin, Natsuki.

240
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:20,200
[JIJIMARU]
You should nap, Natsuki.

241
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,950
[GABBY] Yeah, you heard 'em.

242
00:12:22,030 --> 00:12:23,780
Go straight to bed.

243
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,870
[Natsuki sighs] Hm.

244
00:12:25,950 --> 00:12:27,210
Fine.

245
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:29,750
I'll settle in for some R and R

246
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:31,830
once you've finished
today's problems.

247
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:34,000
Hurry up and solve
all the equations

248
00:12:34,090 --> 00:12:35,380
so I can go relax.

249
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:36,800
[ASA AND GABBY] Monster.

250
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:41,090
[exclaims] Hold on a sec.
Can I use Break on math?

251
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:44,720
Don't use a legendary daemon
on stupid BS like that!

252
00:12:52,190 --> 00:12:53,230
[NATSUKI] Hm?

253
00:12:54,150 --> 00:12:55,940
-[footsteps]
-[FUYUKI] Natsuki.

254
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:02,740
Thirsty? Jin said
we should take the day off.

255
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,120
[Natsuki groans]

256
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:09,460
Haruo, care for a glass?

257
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:11,870
Join us.
We'll drink, then sleep.

258
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:14,710
We can think about Akio
after we've sobered up.

259
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:19,470
Booze and an all-nighter?
That's hell on your skin, dummy.

260
00:13:20,220 --> 00:13:21,300
[Natsuki chuckles]

261
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:24,100
On second thought, let's put you
to sleep right away.

262
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:25,050
Play nice.

263
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:30,560
[Yuru groans]

264
00:13:31,350 --> 00:13:32,230
All right!

265
00:13:32,310 --> 00:13:33,900
What is he doing?

266
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,020
Learning stuff.

267
00:13:35,110 --> 00:13:37,190
I got him
an electronic dictionary

268
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:39,280
to look up words
he doesn't know.

269
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,320
[YURU] Since I came down
the mountain,

270
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:44,200
I've come across a lot of words
I can read but don't understand.

271
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:46,780
Now I don't have to ask people
to explain them to me.

272
00:13:46,870 --> 00:13:49,700
Oh, interesting. So you're using
hiragana mode, huh?

273
00:13:49,790 --> 00:13:50,710
[YURU] Yeah.

274
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:53,460
By the way,
what did you study

275
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:55,330
back when you were still
in the village?

276
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:57,130
[YURU] I read
whatever texts Dera brought

277
00:13:57,210 --> 00:13:58,500
from the outside world.

278
00:13:58,590 --> 00:14:00,050
Sun Tzu and the like.

279
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:01,880
Yuru, you're amazing!

280
00:14:01,970 --> 00:14:03,470
A smart barbarian!

281
00:14:03,550 --> 00:14:06,470
[YURU] I only said I read it,
not that I understood it.

282
00:14:07,350 --> 00:14:08,850
Oh, what?

283
00:14:08,930 --> 00:14:10,680
Is this magic?

284
00:14:10,770 --> 00:14:12,600
[YURU] I honestly have no idea.

285
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:14,230
But it is useful.

286
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:19,940
-Here.
-Thanks so much.

287
00:14:20,030 --> 00:14:22,070
Azami, I'm sure you're confused

288
00:14:22,150 --> 00:14:24,400
after being brought down here
so suddenly.

289
00:14:24,490 --> 00:14:25,870
Are you afraid?

290
00:14:25,950 --> 00:14:28,160
Well, I don't know
what's going on,

291
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:31,950
but I've gotten used to that,
so it's not scary really.

292
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:36,040
Honestly, being super confused
all the time feels normal.

293
00:14:36,130 --> 00:14:37,710
I know just what you mean!

294
00:14:37,790 --> 00:14:39,670
[AZAMI] Also,
the rice here is good.

295
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:41,050
[YURU] I know, right?

296
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:42,590
-[AZAMI] And the cold box...
-This is nice.

297
00:14:42,670 --> 00:14:44,670
Azami seems to be
in good spirits.

298
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:46,640
-[AZAMI] Yeah.
-[YURU] Ah, yes, in the kitchen.

299
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:49,430
Although, I bet she wants
to go back to the village.

300
00:14:49,510 --> 00:14:50,430
[Yuru and Azami chatter]

301
00:14:50,510 --> 00:14:53,640
Where Ma is.
I hope she's okay.

302
00:14:53,730 --> 00:14:54,680
[Right grunts]

303
00:14:54,770 --> 00:14:56,060
Cease your moping.

304
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:57,650
If you walk around
looking gloomy,

305
00:14:57,730 --> 00:14:59,150
you'll scare away your blessing.

306
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:00,770
[BOTH] Left and Right!

307
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:03,400
Oh, hey! Did you both
reattach your limbs?

308
00:15:03,490 --> 00:15:04,650
[RIGHT] Yes.

309
00:15:04,740 --> 00:15:06,610
We are whole once more!

310
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:08,450
But we've yet to fully recover.

311
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:12,250
That said, the stone adhesive
Dera bought did work well.

312
00:15:12,330 --> 00:15:13,660
[RIGHT] We could get
chopped to bits,

313
00:15:13,750 --> 00:15:15,710
and it'd be no problem. [laughs]

314
00:15:16,250 --> 00:15:18,790
Maybe try not
to get anything cut off again.

315
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:20,670
Uh? Hold up.

316
00:15:22,090 --> 00:15:24,220
Where's Dera?
I thought he was here.

317
00:15:26,630 --> 00:15:28,140
[crowd cheering]

318
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,560
Yeah!

319
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:34,430
[groaning]

320
00:15:39,690 --> 00:15:40,570
Mm?

321
00:15:40,650 --> 00:15:42,320
[groans] Mm?

322
00:15:43,190 --> 00:15:46,110
-[DERA] Hey, buddy. Lose big?
-[HAMURA] You, too?

323
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,070
I was hoping for a windfall.

324
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:50,200
Gotta support the kiddos,
you know?

325
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:51,370
Yeah.

326
00:15:51,830 --> 00:15:53,700
I'm out here 'cause I'm hoping
to pay off an old debt.

327
00:15:53,790 --> 00:15:54,910
I even took out a loan

328
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,870
so I'd be able to place
some bigger bets.

329
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,960
But the next race will be ours.

330
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:01,290
You've gotta do right
by those kiddos of yours.

331
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:02,590
Hell yes!

332
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:05,920
[ASA, GABBY AND HANA] Scumbags.

333
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:09,340
[HAMURA] First things first,
time to borrow some more money.

334
00:16:10,550 --> 00:16:11,680
[phone chimes]

335
00:16:14,510 --> 00:16:16,270
Oh, man.

336
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,430
Just great.

337
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:20,230
[DERA] We've been called
to a meeting

338
00:16:20,310 --> 00:16:21,860
of Higashi Village agents.

339
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:23,020
[HANA] They want everyone

340
00:16:23,110 --> 00:16:24,940
with an official position
to be there.

341
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:28,030
Naturally, the message came
from a bandit.

342
00:16:28,110 --> 00:16:29,650
What? Them again?

343
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:32,030
They are definitely planning
to put you through the wringer

344
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:34,160
for the Fujimurayama warehouse
crapfest.

345
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,500
And they are gonna demand
that you hand over Yuru.

346
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:38,040
Yeah, no doubt.

347
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:41,460
Do you want me to go with you
and teach them all a lesson?

348
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:42,920
-I must object.
-Eh?

349
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,670
For real, Yuru, listen to Left.
That's a bad idea.

350
00:16:45,750 --> 00:16:47,550
Since we're not
in top shape yet,

351
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:49,420
we'll have to
sit this fight out.

352
00:16:49,510 --> 00:16:52,470
It wouldn't be wise to hunt down
these knaves by yourself.

353
00:16:52,930 --> 00:16:54,010
Fair point.

354
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:56,390
Then once you're both
fully recovered,

355
00:16:56,470 --> 00:16:58,520
we'll go teach 'em
a lesson together!

356
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,730
[KEN] Don't make it sound
like a party.

357
00:17:00,810 --> 00:17:02,560
A lot of
the Higashi Village agents

358
00:17:02,650 --> 00:17:04,900
who'll be at the meeting
are also Daemon Wielders.

359
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:07,320
You know what that means.
I'll be skipping.

360
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:09,190
What? That's totally unfair.

361
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:10,780
Now if I blow off the meeting,

362
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:13,870
they'll be suspicious
as heck, you bum!

363
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:20,580
What's up, guys?

364
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:22,120
How's it hanging?

365
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:24,130
Ah, Gravedigger.

366
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:25,880
It's good to see you,
Hana babe.

367
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:27,130
You're still alive?

368
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,970
[BANDIT] You hear much
from Tadera these days?

369
00:17:30,050 --> 00:17:31,420
Nope, not a word.

370
00:17:31,510 --> 00:17:34,100
-Why, hasn't he shown up yet?
-No.

371
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:36,850
He hasn't responded to
any of my messages either.

372
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:38,390
Well, that's weird.

373
00:17:38,470 --> 00:17:40,520
If he's gone dark, it could mean
he's hiding something.

374
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:43,560
[BANDIT] When I ran into him
at the Fujimurayama warehouse,

375
00:17:43,650 --> 00:17:45,980
he told me he had no intention
of giving us Yuru

376
00:17:46,070 --> 00:17:48,030
or cooperating with the village.

377
00:17:48,110 --> 00:17:51,700
He betrayed Higashi Village?
I bet that good-for-nothing rat

378
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:54,740
is plotting to use the Seal kid
for his own selfish gain.

379
00:17:54,820 --> 00:17:56,370
He sucks so bad.

380
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:59,410
When we find that steaming turd,
we'll show him what's what.

381
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:02,120
[BANDIT] Jeez.
She really hates him.

382
00:18:02,210 --> 00:18:04,080
-[vehicle approaching]
-[BOTH] Hm?

383
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:08,250
[MALE OFFICIAL]
Ah, the president's here.

384
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:09,510
♪

385
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:24,520
Right, then.
Is everybody present?

386
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:26,400
We're missing Tadera.

387
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:28,480
[PRESIDENT] Hmm, that figures.

388
00:18:29,110 --> 00:18:30,440
[SHIZUKU] Good evening.

389
00:18:30,530 --> 00:18:32,110
[KAGARI]
Lovely to see you again.

390
00:18:32,190 --> 00:18:33,320
[Jiro whines]

391
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,360
[DERA] Ooh!
It's a message from Jiro.

392
00:18:35,450 --> 00:18:36,570
[YURU] President?

393
00:18:37,330 --> 00:18:40,160
The man in charge of
the village's minions down here.

394
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:42,540
He's the one who assigns jobs
to everybody.

395
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:44,750
I'd rather not fight
with the guy.

396
00:18:44,830 --> 00:18:47,340
But he also wants
to control Break and Seal,

397
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:50,590
giving the village
power to rule the world, so...

398
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:53,630
From what I can gather,
Gravedigger,

399
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:56,840
Ryu Tadera has taken Yuru
and disappeared into hiding.

400
00:18:56,930 --> 00:18:58,050
Is that true?

401
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:00,220
Yeah, apparently so.

402
00:19:00,310 --> 00:19:03,220
And you haven't been
in contact with them lately?

403
00:19:03,310 --> 00:19:04,980
It's like I told
the bandits, sir.

404
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:07,610
All I did was bring those
guys down the mountain

405
00:19:07,690 --> 00:19:10,070
and drop them off
somewhere close to Dera's place.

406
00:19:10,150 --> 00:19:11,530
-Haven't heard a peep since.
-[sniffs]

407
00:19:11,610 --> 00:19:13,570
So why didn't you tell us
you took the boy

408
00:19:13,650 --> 00:19:14,690
away from the village?

409
00:19:15,150 --> 00:19:16,650
Don't you think maybe
that's the kind of information

410
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:18,200
you should have
relayed to us immediately?

411
00:19:18,280 --> 00:19:20,620
In fact, if we hadn't talked
to the shaman already,

412
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:21,990
we wouldn't have known
about Yuru

413
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:23,910
or the fact that the village
was being torn apart

414
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:24,910
by enemy forces.

415
00:19:25,210 --> 00:19:26,710
Hey, buddy,
find someone else to blame.

416
00:19:27,460 --> 00:19:30,090
It's not like Dera's been
sharing intel with me either.

417
00:19:30,170 --> 00:19:31,670
[PRESIDENT] Shall we recap?

418
00:19:32,510 --> 00:19:34,340
In the wake
of the horrible attacks,

419
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:36,510
Higashi Village is in shambles.

420
00:19:36,590 --> 00:19:38,130
Yuru is off the mountain,

421
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:41,560
Asa has Break and is under
the influence of the Kagemoris,

422
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,970
and the bandits
took heavy losses.

423
00:19:44,060 --> 00:19:46,100
With Tadera and the Shaman gone,

424
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:48,730
few people know how to get
through the village barrier.

425
00:19:48,810 --> 00:19:51,190
I think you'll all agree
we've found ourselves

426
00:19:51,270 --> 00:19:54,730
in a dire situation
for which I offer a solution.

427
00:19:54,820 --> 00:19:56,530
We can't keep waiting for orders

428
00:19:56,610 --> 00:19:58,030
-from Granny Yamaha.
-[Jiro sniffs]

429
00:19:58,110 --> 00:20:00,740
It would slow us down
and make failure more likely.

430
00:20:00,830 --> 00:20:02,490
[president groans]

431
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:05,410
From now on, I think it's best
that I take over command

432
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:07,660
of our operations down here.

433
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:10,210
[YURU] "Ulterior motives"?

434
00:20:10,290 --> 00:20:13,170
Huh? What?
The old man's after Hana?

435
00:20:13,250 --> 00:20:14,760
Good luck, creep.
She'll kill you!

436
00:20:16,550 --> 00:20:17,550
Oh, hmm.

437
00:20:18,010 --> 00:20:20,760
He meant that kind
of ulterior motive. Much better.

438
00:20:20,850 --> 00:20:23,510
[PRESIDENT] Our first order
of business is to find Tadera

439
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:25,560
and figure out
where he's stashed Yuru.

440
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:26,810
[FEMALE OFFICIAL]
What if he resists?

441
00:20:26,890 --> 00:20:29,020
We can take him down
without a fight easy.

442
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:31,560
He doesn't have daemons,
so we'll just throw ours at him.

443
00:20:31,650 --> 00:20:33,320
-[Jiro grunts]
-Jiro?

444
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,610
-[Jiro grunts]
-[HANA] What did you find?

445
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:42,780
Come here, take a look.

446
00:20:42,870 --> 00:20:44,200
Seems harmless enough.

447
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:47,410
They're daemon relics, right?

448
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:48,910
[SHIZUKU] Correct.

449
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,830
[KAGARI] They're active daemons.

450
00:20:50,920 --> 00:20:53,460
We sense souls within them.

451
00:20:53,840 --> 00:20:55,880
Okay, so who do they
belong to, then?

452
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,210
And why are they
in this warehouse?

453
00:20:58,300 --> 00:20:59,380
No clue.

454
00:20:59,470 --> 00:21:01,590
Someone could form a contract
with them.

455
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:02,680
[all gasp]

456
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:04,310
♪

457
00:21:09,310 --> 00:21:10,310
[Jiro barks]

458
00:21:15,020 --> 00:21:17,400
[♪ closing theme song playing]

459
00:22:45,610 --> 00:22:47,530
[GONZO]
A daemon who infects relics

460
00:22:47,620 --> 00:22:49,450
and causes them to explode.

461
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:51,740
We need more intel.

462
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:53,410
Know anything?

463
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:56,960
I have no information
on anyone with such abilities.

464
00:22:57,040 --> 00:22:59,590
Then we're dealing with a power
that's unknown to us.

465
00:23:00,130 --> 00:23:01,960
Let's make sure everybody
in the manor

466
00:23:02,050 --> 00:23:03,550
checks their daemons at once.

467
00:23:03,630 --> 00:23:04,840
They could be infected.

468
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:06,630
Bunbun had an idea.

469
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:08,970
It's possibly a daemon
from the West.

470
00:23:09,430 --> 00:23:11,430
The West. Hm...

471
00:23:12,310 --> 00:23:13,890
Perhaps...

472
00:23:13,980 --> 00:23:16,100
No, it couldn't be.

473
00:23:17,310 --> 00:23:19,570
Nishino Village was destroyed.

474
00:23:19,650 --> 00:23:23,230
A drowned corpse
at the bottom of a reservoir.
